ions we  will finally see what all these letters  mean this owl-like creature is obviously  a powerful deity that could be as major  as a goddess hylia or some other  important figure entirely this part gets  a little tougher to figure out we now  see two figures and two scenes these are  both very likely Zelda or descendant  with the ears and the dress we then see  Zelda cupping her hand with the same  owl-like creature below two tiers we  know this because the same shot pans out  later in the trailer this is obviously  all within deep breath of the wild lore  that just hasn't been revealed yet so  the name of the game here is to take  things at face value and keep them in  your mind until we finally see the truth  unfold now we get to the juicy part we  see link open up a pair pair of massive  doors out into the new Sky area these  doors themselves have intricate designs  of two zonai creatures and with what  looks like a chica eye symbol on the  bottom of the door as well which still  supports the previous idea of the zona's  link to Shiga history this imagery of  the two dragons here also holds  similarities to the hand cupping shown  in the wall designs before we then  finally get a close-up of Link still  donning his amazing highly in tunic  Champions tunic hybrid outfit with the  huge Stone building behind him what's  cool about this shot specifically though  is that this is the first time that we  see these close up in the sky this  finally gives Clarity to the situation  as we previously thought that  long-haired link was purely tied to the  sky only and that there would have to be  time travel between land and sky but  because he is here in this date and with  more shots later in the trailer it's  confirmed that this is one cohesive  world with no State change or loading  between land and Sky you can also see  something located on his hip with what  looks like some sort of ammo belt but  it's unknown exactly what this was for  looking closely though you can see that  this is a zonai designed eye at the top  of the device with containers of light  green energy we associate with the zonai  thinking about it more though if these  containers are placed below the eye like  this these are indeed an idea of a  teardrop this lines up with the fact  that this was simply omitted in previous  trailers and Nintendo clearly stated  that when they reveal the name it will  spoil some aspects of the game so the  choice to reveal it now must link to the  name what doesn't add up though is there  eight container slots not lining up with  the seven tiers surrounding the  important deity shown before so it is  completely unclear on the purpose of  this strange device he then dives off  the edge into Open Sky this is actually  the exact same animation in breath of  the wild for diving into water from high  up but then transitions into the  skydiving animation that they've been  holding back for possibly a decade at  this point remember this skydiving  animation was initially an idea in the  original breath of the wild an imported  idea from a Skyward Sword but of course  is coming in full swing in the sequel  then we see one of the more interesting  Parts link climbs onto a stone slab and  soars upwards with the boulder first  this location is at Corda Lake in the  Faron region in this four pillared zonai  Contraption in the water well my  favorite piece of information about this  trailer is that it sets up the  possibility for rebuilding or fixing the  sky using these pieces from below for  puzzling and exploration think about it  it's clear that from a previous trailer  that the skill with the yellow outline  is a Time reversal mechanic so this must  mean that this piece has fallen  previously from the sky this also May  subtly refer to the title of the entire  game tears of the Kingdom will make a  heck of a lot of sense if the kingdom  was ancient land above and the tears or  tares both work in a situation where  pieces that fell down likely due to a  catastrophic event which was probably  not filled with happy times we also see  a brand new enemy or Wildlife a strange  bat-like creature much larger than a  standard keys but we still have no idea  what it is this next shot supports but  doesn't entirely 100 confirm what I  suspected last year I previously they  said that these islands in the sky have  walls that are severely unfriendly for  climbing similar to Shrine walls you may  not be able to grip onto we see  long-haired link here climbing only the  root on the wall which may support this  Theory we again have to see more footage  to confirm this fact we finally see the  widest shot of the new Hyrule we've seen  so far because of the harsh lighting of  the sunset details are hard to point out  but this shot makes it very clear the  scale of How High these different  Islands actually are another thing is  we've been here before in the previous  trailer we were shown tons of islands  above the Thunder of plateau where we're  dropping down right now but none of  these large islands from before seem to  show up in the right places so this  likely shows that these islands are  things that appear or disappear  depending on some context were still  missing link then transfers from the  skydiving position into the normal  falling position it's unclear at this  point if this is a scripted animation  path to perfectly fall onto this glider  or if this is how the game works in  general with all skydiving detecting how  close you are to the ground before  automatically tilting link to a normal  all this also May prevent comedic  splatting which will be a bummer because  I miss this hilarious interaction from a  Skyward Sword  but we still haven't seen him land on  Solid Ground yet so we'll see in the  future we also see several huge zonai  designs on the ground both at North  Hyrule plain and at the illumini plateau  in this case specifically this sort of  makes sense since the base word is  illuminate which means to light up what  it does specifically though we have yet  to know there's also this spiral  structure here just north of the panther  Bridge stable there's no way to tell  what this is from far away but it does  have a fairly similar spiral design to  the unraveling hand holding down Ganon  from the very first trailer and of  course this Stone glider is the very  last thing we see if you don't believe  me about the Ghibli references yet well  here's another one nausicaa's glider we  don't know if it's fully controllable  but judging by how it's already moving  when link gets there it's hard to say we  finally then see the game name with the  corrupted Master Sword we saw before and  what appears to be two dragons or zonai  creatures in a Circle what's interesting  about this layout is that Nintendo  doesn't Implement stuff just to look  cool these things have a hidden meaning  a snake eating itself or two snakes  eating each other in Greek mythology is  represented as oroboros the cycle of  Life Death and rebirth while it's hard  to decipher what exactly this means  right now I feel like at a minimum this  should be kept in the back of your mind  as we get more information about the  story of The Legend of Zelda tears of  the Kingdom  what are you most excited about with  tears of the Kingdom let us know in the  comments below and to make sure to keep  up with everything Zelda stay tuned with  us here on Gamespot  foreign  [Music]

